@startuml
package "Client/Editor Layer" {
  component "Browser Editor\n(TypeScript/React SPA)" as BrowserEditor
  component "Layout Editing Interface" as LayoutEditor
  component "Canvas Render/Delete Operations" as CanvasOps
  component "Redux Store" as ReduxStore
  component "Controls Slice" as ControlsSlice
  component "Elements Slice" as ElementsSlice
  component "Layouts Slice" as LayoutsSlice
  component "Gauges Slice" as GaugesSlice
  component "Displays Slice\n(Client Display State)" as ClientDisplayState
}

package "API/Server Layer" {
  component "Django Server\n(Python/Django, API resources)" as DjangoServer
  component "Django Dev Startup\n(./manage.py runserver)" as DjangoDevStartup
  component "Gauge Resource" as GaugeResource
  component "Display Resource" as DisplayResource
  component "Layout Resource" as LayoutResource
  component "Static Asset Serving" as StaticAssetServing
}

package "Viewer/Rendering Layer" {
  component "Viewer" as Viewer
}

package "Data/Persistence Layer" {
  database "PostgreSQL Database" as Postgres
}

package "Build/Deployment/Environment Layer" {
  component "Build Pipeline\n(npm install / npm run build)" as BuildPipeline
  component "Python Package Installation\n(pip/requirements)" as PythonPackageInstall
  node "Docker/Container Runtime" as DockerRuntime
  node "Python 3.7 Runtime" as PythonRuntime
  node "Node.js/npm Runtime" as NodeNpm
}

package "External Systems" {
  node "Browser" as Browser
  node "OLED Displays" as OLED
  node "E-paper Displays" as Epaper
  node "LCD Displays" as LCD
  component "API Clients" as APIClients
}

Browser --> BrowserEditor : hosts
Browser --> Viewer : accesses viewer
Browser --> StaticAssetServing : loads built editor assets
BrowserEditor --> ReduxStore : uses state
ReduxStore --> ControlsSlice : manages
ReduxStore --> ElementsSlice : manages
ReduxStore --> LayoutsSlice : manages
ReduxStore --> GaugesSlice : manages
ReduxStore --> ClientDisplayState : manages displays state
BrowserEditor --> LayoutEditor : provides editing UI
LayoutEditor --> CanvasOps : invokes render/delete
LayoutEditor --> LayoutsSlice : composes layouts across displays
LayoutEditor --> ElementsSlice : edits elements
LayoutEditor --> ClientDisplayState : targets displays
BrowserEditor --> DjangoServer : REST/API
LayoutEditor --> DjangoServer : persists layout/display changes (REST/API)
APIClients --> DjangoServer : API usage

DjangoServer --> GaugeResource : exposes
DjangoServer --> DisplayResource : exposes
DjangoServer --> LayoutResource : exposes
DjangoServer --> Postgres : persists Gauge/Display/Layout
DisplayResource --> LayoutResource : current_layout
LayoutResource ..> DisplayResource : on delete sets current_layout = null (DR-009)
DjangoServer --> StaticAssetServing : serves built assets
DockerRuntime --> DjangoDevStartup : starts
DjangoDevStartup --> DjangoServer : runs
DjangoServer --> PythonRuntime : runs on
DjangoServer --> PythonPackageInstall : depends on installed packages

Viewer --> DisplayResource : reads display_data
Viewer --> LayoutResource : reads layout/display_positions
Viewer --> OLED : renders B/W pixels
Viewer --> Epaper : renders B/W pixels
Viewer --> LCD : renders B/W pixels
Viewer --> Browser : renders browser display target

BuildPipeline --> NodeNpm : npm install / npm run build
BuildPipeline --> StaticAssetServing : produces built client assets
DockerRuntime --> BuildPipeline : runs build steps
DockerRuntime --> PythonPackageInstall : installs Python packages
PythonPackageInstall --> PythonRuntime : installs into
DockerRuntime --> Postgres : runs

DisplayResource ..> ClientDisplayState : source-of-truth fields mirrored in client (conceptual)

note right of DjangoDevStartup
  Development-grade / non-production
  (C-005, C-006, NFR-004)
end note
@enduml
